      },
      "ordering_key": 1,
      "per_curiam": false,
      "sha1": "",
      "snippet": "\nThe issue in this case is whether the Persistent Offender Accountability Act (the two-strike statute), chapter 9.94A\nRCW, for sex offenders includes prior convictions (strikes) which were not specifically listed when Delgado was tried and sentenced for his current offense. We hold that the two-strike statute was unambiguous and did not include any offenses other than those specifically listed. We reverse the Court of Appeals and affirm the sentence i",
